ipedia/commons/6/66/Oreochromis_niloticus_%28RFEIMG-0352%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oreochromis_niloticus_(RFEIMG-0352).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=164913463","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2025-05-08 08:13:47","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Oreochromis niloticus (RFEIMG-0352)","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Center for Food Safety and Applied Nutrition|PD US FDA|Images from the United States Food and Drug Administration|Flickr images reviewed by FlickreviewR 2|Seafood products","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"The Regulatory Fish Encyclopedia (RFE) project (1993-2000) was a compilation of data in several formats to assist with the accurate identification of fish species. It was developed by FDA's RFE Team of scientists at the (former) Seafood Products Research Center, Seattle District, and the (former) Center for Food Safety and Applied Nutrition to help federal, state, and local officials and purchasers of seafood identify species substitution and economic deception in the marketplace. The RFE included high-resolution photographs for a number of commercially relevant fish species for sale in the U.S. market. The scanned digital images include whole fish as well as their marketed product forms such as fillets, steaks, etc.\nImages used in the RFE were photographed on a modified Polaroid MP4 camera system fitted with a Polaroid 545 holder for 4\" x 5\" film, and a 135 mm lens. Quickload tungsten-balanced ISO 64 E-6 process 4\" x 5\" transparency film was used to capture the images. A 10 cm scale bar was included in each photograph to indicate specimen size and magnification, and a standard Kodak color bar was included to assure color accuracy. Developed transparencies were professionally scanned to produce the digitized graphic images provided here.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2024-06-12 20:09:48","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/39736050@N02/54451757816/\">https://www.flickr.com/photos/39736050@N02/54451757816/</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"The U.S. Food and Drug Administration","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"164913461":{"pageid":164913461,"ns":6,"title":"File:Oreochromis niloticus (RFEIMG-0354).jpg","index":3,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Oreochromis_niloticus_%28RFEIMG-0354%29.jpg/500px-Oreochromis_niloticus_%28RFEIMG-0354%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":400,"thumbheight":303,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Oreochromis_niloticus_%28RFEIMG-0354%29.jpg/960px-Oreochromis_niloticus_%28RFEIMG-0354%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Oreochromis_niloticus_%28RFEIMG-0354%29.jpg/500px-Oreochromis_niloticus_%28RFEIMG-0354%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":400,"height":303,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Oreochromis_niloticus_%28RFEIMG-0354%29.jpg/960px-Oreochromis_niloticus_%28RFEIMG-0354%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/98/Oreochromis_niloticus_%28RFEIMG-0354%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oreochromis_niloticus_(RFEIMG-0354).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=164913461","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2025-05-08 08:13:44","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Oreochromis niloticus (RFEIMG-0354)","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Center for Food Safety and Applied Nutrition|PD US FDA|Images from the United States Food and Drug Administration|Flickr images reviewed by FlickreviewR 2|Seafood products|Flickr images missing SDC published in","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"The Regulatory Fish Encyclopedia (RFE) project (1993-2000) was a compilation of data in several formats to assist with the accurate identification of fish species. It was developed by FDA's RFE Team of scientists at the (former) Seafood Products Research Center, Seattle District, and the (former) Center for Food Safety and Applied Nutrition to help federal, state, and local officials and purchasers of seafood identify species substitution and economic deception in the marketplace. The RFE included high-resolution photographs for a number of commercially relevant fish species for sale in the U.S. market. The scanned digital images include whole fish as well as their marketed product forms such as fillets, steaks, etc.\nImages used in the RFE were photographed on a modified Polaroid MP4 camera system fitted with a Polaroid 545 holder for 4\" x 5\" film, and a 135 mm lens. Quickload tungsten-balanced ISO 64 E-6 process 4\" x 5\" transparency film was used to capture the images. A 10 cm scale bar was included in each photograph to indicate specimen size and magnification, and a standard Kodak color bar was included to assure color accuracy. Developed transparencies were professionally scanned to produce the digitized graphic images provided here.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2024-06-12 20:12:03","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/39736050@N02/54451754411/\">https://www.flickr.com/photos/39736050@N02/54451754411/</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"The U.S. Food and Drug Administration","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"18988058":{"pageid":18988058,"ns":6,"title":"File:Oreochromis niloticus at Kanchanaburi market.jpg","index":1,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Oreochromis_niloticus_at_Kanchanaburi_market.jpg/500px-Oreochromis_niloticus_at_Kanchanaburi_market.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":400,"thumbheight":533,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Oreochromis_niloticus_at_Kanchanaburi_market.jpg/960px-Oreochromi